[2026-11-21 23:22:02] Class II caveats, in order of how much they matter:
[2026-11-21 23:22:02]   1. DP and DQ are heterodimers but the IEDB file stores chain frequencies, so molecule coverage is bracketed, not computed. Both bounds are reported.
[2026-11-21 23:22:02]   2. Populations differ in which class II loci were typed. A population with no HLA-DRB1 entry cannot be scored at DR, and is NOT a population with zero DR coverage; summary statistics therefore cover only the populations typed at all five presenting loci, and every row carries loci_typed and scorable.
[2026-11-21 23:22:02]   3. HLA-DRB3/4/5 have no frequency data in this file, so 4 of the 27 panel alleles cannot contribute and the DR term is DRB1-only.
[2026-11-21 23:22:02]   4. Coverage reflects the ALLELE PANEL, not epitope quality: with 22,624 peptides every allele has some predicted binder, so these figures are close to the panel's maximum and are not a property of the shortlist.
[2026-11-21 23:22:02]   5. No class II predictor is benchmarked in this study.
[2026-11-21 23:22:02] 
[2026-11-21 23:22:02] Caveat: HLA-C is absent from the step15 panel, so combined class I coverage is conservative.
